      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1,700 mg three times daily adds up to **5,100 mg of metformin per day**. The usual maximum is **2,550 mg/day** for immediate-release metformin (often given as 850 mg three times daily) and **2,000 mg/day** for extended-release. This order is about twice the immediate-release maximum and raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe stomach and bowel side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What may have been meant:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day, a common target dose)\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release, and I'll enter it right away. If you meant 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
